               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate calendar="#gregorian" notAfter="1459" notBefore="1440" when-custom="144X/145X">s. xv med.</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#d"><orgName key="org_299" role="fmo">Leicester, Leicestershire. Augustinian abbey of St Mary the Veirgin de Pratis</orgName>
                     <p>The secundo folio, 'sit molestus' (fol. 7r, after the tabula) is a match for the entry in the library catalogue of the Leicester Austins, A20.646, where the copy is said to be <q>in magno uolumine</q>. This book is 410 × 270 mm (Freeman, 79–80, 119–20, 240–1).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Ralph Seyton, canon of Leicester and student at Oxford in 1440, who gave the book to his house. (See further BRUO 1676.) According to the library catalogue he was the donor of ten or eleven other volumes (A20. 466, 467, 480, 646, 1009, 1042, 1043, 1045, 1330, 1331 and perhaps 1102 ('per Radulphum')).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Humfrey Ridinge, s. xvi. (A kinsman of Hector Riddinge who had A20.660 in 1503?)</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sir Henry Savile of Banke (1568–1617).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Purchased for Chester Cathedral in 1924 or 1925; their MS 2.</provenance>
               </history>
